WEBVTT

00:10.010 --> 00:11.970
[gasping and sputtering]

00:23.189 --> 00:24.357
Hello?

00:28.319 --> 00:29.529
Nancy?

00:32.323 --> 00:33.616
Nancy!

00:35.243 --> 00:36.453
[shouts] Hello?

00:37.787 --> 00:40.081
- [growling]
- [screaming]

00:46.629 --> 00:48.089
[whimpering] Oh, my God...

00:48.173 --> 00:49.382
[shrieks]

00:53.136 --> 00:55.346
- [monster growling]
- [Barbara grunting]

00:56.639 --> 00:58.141
Nancy!

00:58.224 --> 00:59.267
[voice echoes]

01:01.978 --> 01:03.354
Hey, what's the matter?

01:04.773 --> 01:06.441
Nothing.

01:06.524 --> 01:08.693
[growling continues]

01:10.737 --> 01:12.155
[groaning]

01:14.866 --> 01:16.159
[straining]

01:17.952 --> 01:18.953
[yelps]

01:21.915 --> 01:23.249
[screams]

01:27.712 --> 01:29.589
- [shrieking]
- [growling continues]

01:32.592 --> 01:33.760
[screaming]

01:35.220 --> 01:36.596
You're so beautiful.

01:39.015 --> 01:40.517
- [screaming]
- [growling continues]

01:43.853 --> 01:45.355
[shrieking] Nancy!

01:46.356 --> 01:49.150
[low growling]

02:01.162 --> 02:03.164
[theme music playing]

03:26.247 --> 03:27.498
Steve?

03:30.376 --> 03:32.503
- Hey, Steve.
- Mmm.

03:35.048 --> 03:36.257
I'll...

03:37.675 --> 03:39.302
see you tomorrow, okay?

03:41.429 --> 03:42.430
Mmm-hmm.

04:01.032 --> 04:02.283
[owl hooting]

04:16.798 --> 04:18.633
Oh! Jesus, you scared me.

04:18.716 --> 04:19.884
Oh, I scared you?

04:19.968 --> 04:21.177
I know, I should have called.

04:21.261 --> 04:22.845
[loudly] Where have you been?

04:22.929 --> 04:24.389
[softly] We agreed on 10:00.

04:24.472 --> 04:27.433
After the assembly, some people
wanted to get something to eat.

04:27.517 --> 04:28.518
I didn't think it'd be a big deal.

04:28.601 --> 04:30.770
You didn't think to call and let me know?

04:30.853 --> 04:32.522
With everything that's been going on?

04:32.605 --> 04:35.358
I didn't realize how late it was, okay?

04:35.441 --> 04:37.193
I'm sorry, Mom.
What more do you want?

04:37.277 --> 04:38.569
Hey, wait...

04:38.653 --> 04:39.821
Whose sweatshirt is that?

04:41.572 --> 04:42.573
Steve's.

04:42.657 --> 04:44.367
Steve's.

04:45.535 --> 04:46.703
So is Steve your boyfriend now?

04:46.786 --> 04:48.079
What?

04:48.162 --> 04:49.163
No!

04:49.247 --> 04:52.292
It was just cold,
so I borrowed his sweatshirt.

04:52.375 --> 04:53.626
It's not a big deal.

04:54.627 --> 04:55.878
Nancy?

04:55.962 --> 04:57.547
What?

04:59.048 --> 05:01.009
You can talk to me.

05:01.092 --> 05:03.970
You can talk to me.
Whatever happened.

05:04.053 --> 05:06.764
Nothing happened.

05:09.225 --> 05:10.768
Nancy.

05:12.687 --> 05:14.689
Nothing happened.

05:16.649 --> 05:18.151
Can I please go?

05:30.079 --> 05:31.664
[swing creaking]

05:43.051 --> 05:45.011
[Joyce softly] Will? Will?

05:46.512 --> 05:48.765
Sweetheart, can you hear me?

05:48.848 --> 05:49.849
Will...

05:49.932 --> 05:51.184
Please...

05:51.267 --> 05:52.894
Will...

05:52.977 --> 05:54.020
[grunts]

05:54.937 --> 05:55.980
It's me.

05:56.898 --> 05:59.567
It's me. Just talk to me.
Talk to me.

05:59.650 --> 06:01.652
Just say... [stammers]

06:01.736 --> 06:03.905
- Mom?
- Jonathan!

06:03.988 --> 06:06.866
- [stammering] Come here. Come here.
- Mom, what is this?

06:06.949 --> 06:09.494
Come here. Come here.
[sniffles]

06:09.577 --> 06:11.913
- What's going on?
- It's Will. It's Will, he's...

06:11.996 --> 06:13.831
he's trying to talk to me.

06:13.915 --> 06:15.792
[breath trembling]

06:15.875 --> 06:19.003
- He's trying to talk to you?
- Yes, through... through the lights.

06:19.087 --> 06:20.213
- Mom--
- I know.

06:20.296 --> 06:21.672
I know.

06:21.756 --> 06:23.883
Just... just watch.

06:23.966 --> 06:27.553
Will... your brother's here.

06:29.013 --> 06:31.432
Can you show him what you showed me, baby?

06:33.768 --> 06:35.311
Please...
[gasps] Did you see that?

06:35.394 --> 06:37.355
It's the electricity, Mom.

06:37.438 --> 06:38.689
- [stammering] It's acting up.
- No.

06:38.773 --> 06:40.358
It's the same thing that fried the phone.

06:40.441 --> 06:42.985
No! It is not the electricity, Jonathan.

06:43.069 --> 06:45.279
Something is going on here!

06:45.363 --> 06:47.990
- Yesterday, the wall--
- What? What about the wall?

06:48.074 --> 06:50.243
- I don't know. I don't know.
- Mom, first the lights, then the wall?

06:50.326 --> 06:52.703
[stammers] I just know that Will is here.

06:52.787 --> 06:54.288
- [sighs]
- No, Mom.

06:54.372 --> 06:57.041
- [stammering] Maybe if I get more lamps--
- No, Mom.

06:57.125 --> 07:01.546
You don't need more lamps.
You need to stop this, okay?

07:01.629 --> 07:03.798
He is just lost.

07:03.881 --> 07:07.969
People are looking for him,
and they're going to find him.

07:08.052 --> 07:09.637
[stammering] Okay.

07:09.720 --> 07:11.931
- This isn't helping.
- Okay, okay.

07:12.014 --> 07:14.308
Okay, I'm sorry.
[sniffling] I'm sorry.

07:15.101 --> 07:16.644
Can you do me a favor, Mom?

07:16.727 --> 07:18.479
Can you just try and get some sleep?

07:18.563 --> 07:21.232
- [sniffling] Yeah.
- Huh? Can you do that for me?

07:21.315 --> 07:22.567
- I promise. I will.
- Yeah?

07:22.650 --> 07:24.610
- Yeah.
- I just need to sit here for a minute.

07:24.694 --> 07:25.695
[sniffles]

07:25.778 --> 07:27.572
All right, I'll go make breakfast.

07:27.655 --> 07:29.157
- Okay.
- Yeah?

07:29.240 --> 07:30.450
[Jonathan sighs]

07:39.542 --> 07:40.751
[whispers] Will?

07:42.170 --> 07:44.297
[radio static]

07:44.380 --> 07:46.841
We just tell our parents
we have AV Club after school.

07:46.924 --> 07:49.510
That'll give us at least a few hours
for Operation Mirkwood.

07:50.553 --> 07:53.139
You seriously think that
the weirdo knows where Will is?

07:53.222 --> 07:54.932
- Just trust me on this, okay?
- Okay.

07:55.016 --> 07:56.517
- Did you get the supplies?
- Yeah.

07:56.601 --> 07:59.228
Binoculars... from 'Nam.

07:59.312 --> 08:01.481
Army knife... also from 'Nam.

08:01.564 --> 08:04.025
Hammer, camouflage bandana...

08:04.108 --> 08:06.277
and the wrist rocket.

08:06.360 --> 08:08.362
You're gonna take out the Demogorgon
with a slingshot?

08:08.446 --> 08:10.907
First of all, it's a wrist rocket.

08:10.990 --> 08:13.326
And second of all,
the Demogorgon's not real.

08:13.409 --> 08:14.410
It's made up.

08:14.494 --> 08:17.747
But if there is something out there,
I'm gonna shoot it in the eye...

08:19.040 --> 08:21.501
- and blind it.
- [sighs] Dustin, what did you get?

08:25.421 --> 08:26.589
Well, alrighty.

08:26.672 --> 08:27.924
So, we've got...

08:28.007 --> 08:31.385
Nutty Bars, Bazooka, Pez, Smarties,

08:31.469 --> 08:34.013
Pringles, Nilla Wafers, apple,

08:34.096 --> 08:36.265
- banana, and trail mix.
- Seriously?

08:36.349 --> 08:38.851
We need energy for our travels.
For stamina.

08:38.935 --> 08:41.062
And besides, why do we
even need weapons anyway?

08:41.145 --> 08:43.773
- We have her.
- [Lucas] She shut one door!

08:43.856 --> 08:45.024
With her mind!

08:45.107 --> 08:47.777
Are you kidding me?
That's insane!

08:47.860 --> 08:50.738
Imagine all the other cool stuff
she could do.

08:50.821 --> 08:51.906
Like...

08:52.782 --> 08:56.452
I bet... that she could make this fly!

08:58.788 --> 09:00.164
Hey. Hey.

09:00.248 --> 09:01.832
Okay, concentrate.
Okay?

09:02.500 --> 09:03.751
[clatters]

09:03.834 --> 09:05.211
Okay, one more time.

09:06.420 --> 09:08.548
- Okay.
- [sighs]

09:08.631 --> 09:10.341
Use your powers, okay?

09:10.424 --> 09:11.926
[clatters]

09:12.009 --> 09:13.427
- Idiot.
- [Mike sighs]

09:13.511 --> 09:15.179
- She's not a dog!
- [Karen] Boys!

09:15.263 --> 09:17.014
Time for school!

09:19.183 --> 09:20.226
Just stay down here.

09:20.309 --> 09:22.562
Don't make any noise,
and don't leave.

09:22.687 --> 09:25.106
If you get hungry,
eat Dustin's snacks, okay?

09:25.189 --> 09:27.066
- [Karen] Michael!
- Coming!

09:27.149 --> 09:28.526
You know those power lines?

09:28.609 --> 09:30.403
- Power lines?
- Yeah.

09:30.486 --> 09:31.529
The ones behind my house?

09:31.612 --> 09:32.822
Yes.

09:32.905 --> 09:34.448
Meet us there, after school.

09:34.532 --> 09:36.200
After school?

09:36.284 --> 09:37.618
Yeah, 3:15.

09:39.745 --> 09:40.830
Ah.

09:46.711 --> 09:49.505
When the numbers read three-one-five,
meet us there.

09:49.589 --> 09:51.799
"Three-one-five."

09:51.882 --> 09:53.843
Three-one-five.

09:58.889 --> 10:00.600
[footsteps receding]

10:01.350 --> 10:03.102
[indistinct chatter]

10:20.119 --> 10:21.412
Hey!

10:21.495 --> 10:22.580
[laughs nervously] Hey!

10:23.539 --> 10:25.166
- Is everything okay?
- Yeah!

10:25.249 --> 10:26.709
Yeah, totally.

10:27.710 --> 10:28.794
I just...

10:30.421 --> 10:33.215
I feel like everyone's... staring at me.

10:33.299 --> 10:34.800
Oh, I didn't... I didn't tell anyone.

10:34.884 --> 10:36.135
I know.

10:36.218 --> 10:38.054
I know.
Of course not.

10:38.763 --> 10:41.682
But what about, like, Tommy,
and Carol and them?

10:41.766 --> 10:42.850
You're being paranoid.

10:43.851 --> 10:46.312
- I'm sorry.
- No. No, it's cute.

10:48.522 --> 10:49.523
Hey...

10:49.607 --> 10:51.275
I had a good time.

10:53.152 --> 10:54.320
Yeah.

10:55.613 --> 10:57.114
Yeah.
Me, too.

11:06.374 --> 11:07.792
[both chuckle softly]

11:09.669 --> 11:11.087
Mmm.
Hmm.

11:16.801 --> 11:18.469
[indistinct chatter]

11:23.099 --> 11:24.809
[bell rings]

11:27.686 --> 11:29.563
Hey, Ally.
Where's Barb?

11:29.647 --> 11:31.482
Um, shouldn't you know?

11:31.565 --> 11:33.734
You haven't seen her anywhere...
at all?

11:39.448 --> 11:41.992
[Powell] There she is.
Emerald City.

11:42.076 --> 11:44.203
[Callahan] I heard they make
space weapons in there.

11:44.286 --> 11:45.287
[Powell] Space weapons?

11:45.371 --> 11:47.498
[Callahan] Yeah. You know, like,
Reagan's Star Wars.

11:47.581 --> 11:50.251
I guess we're gonna blow
the Ruskies to smithereens.

11:51.585 --> 11:52.586
[guard] Hey, can I help you?

11:53.629 --> 11:55.631
Uh, yeah.
We're here for a tour.

11:55.714 --> 11:57.508
Oh, we don't give tours.

11:57.591 --> 11:59.635
Okay...
A quick look around.

11:59.718 --> 12:02.346
You have to get clearance for that.
You can contact, uh...

12:02.430 --> 12:04.014
Rick Schaeffer
at the Department of Energy.

12:04.098 --> 12:06.183
Maybe you seen it on TV.
We got a local kid that's missing.

12:06.267 --> 12:08.102
We have reason to believe
he might have snuck in here.

12:08.185 --> 12:10.646
Like I said,
you have to speak to Mr. Schaeffer.

12:10.729 --> 12:11.897
[engine cuts out]

12:13.107 --> 12:14.942
- What's your name?
- Patrick.

12:15.025 --> 12:18.612
Patrick, I got a panicked mayor,
and I got reporters breathing down my neck

12:18.696 --> 12:20.281
and I got a very upset mother.

12:21.699 --> 12:25.870
Now, I know the kid's not in there,
but I gotta check off this box.

12:27.788 --> 12:30.166
Patrick, would you do me a favor?

12:30.249 --> 12:33.794
Would you speak to your boss
and see what you can swing for us?

12:35.045 --> 12:36.380
I'd really appreciate it.

12:37.339 --> 12:39.341
I'm talking ten minutes, tops.

12:57.193 --> 12:58.319
[clatters]

13:01.280 --> 13:02.781
[static crackling]

13:29.892 --> 13:31.560
[dial tone]

13:36.524 --> 13:38.317
[mimicking dial tone]

13:49.578 --> 13:52.498
[Ronald Reagan]
...was occupying a large part of Lebanon.

13:52.581 --> 13:54.750
Today, Syria has become a home for--

13:57.294 --> 13:59.964
[He-Man] I have the power!

14:00.047 --> 14:01.674
[announcer]
...gift that will last forever.

14:01.757 --> 14:03.926
From the Harmony Treasures' collection--

14:04.009 --> 14:05.761
[gospel music playing]

14:07.304 --> 14:08.889
- [flips channel]
- [jingle playing]

14:10.391 --> 14:13.602
[woman singing]
♪ On the beach and in the sun ♪

14:13.686 --> 14:16.730
♪ The real thing is so much fun ♪

14:16.814 --> 14:20.484
♪ All the times of your life
And the things that you do ♪

14:20.568 --> 14:23.279
♪ Coke is right there with you ♪

14:26.907 --> 14:28.951
- [devices humming]
- [machine beeping]

14:38.961 --> 14:40.212
[straining]

14:45.885 --> 14:48.762
[monitors beeping rapidly]

14:50.055 --> 14:51.599
[breathing heavily]

15:00.733 --> 15:01.901
[gasps]

15:13.162 --> 15:14.538
[jingle playing on TV]

15:14.622 --> 15:17.875
[woman singing]
♪ Coke is it! Coke is it! ♪

15:42.816 --> 15:44.276
[whimpers]

16:20.437 --> 16:21.647
[sighs]

16:21.730 --> 16:22.982
[Christmas carol playing]

16:23.065 --> 16:24.775
[sighing]

16:36.120 --> 16:39.373
- [sighs] Joyce--
- Just ring me up, Donald.

16:39.456 --> 16:42.501
And you think this missing boy
may have crawled through there?

16:42.584 --> 16:45.212
[Hopper] Well, that was the idea.

16:45.295 --> 16:47.715
Yeah, I just don't see
how that'd be possible.

16:47.798 --> 16:49.508
We've got over 100 cameras.

16:49.591 --> 16:52.219
Every square inch covered,
plus all my guys.

16:52.928 --> 16:54.388
No one breaks in here.

16:54.471 --> 16:56.098
Certainly not some kid.

16:56.181 --> 16:58.600
Those cameras, you keep the tapes?

17:04.314 --> 17:06.567
[Hopper] If you don't mind me asking,
what do you guys do in here?

17:06.650 --> 17:08.402
[chuckles] You're asking the wrong guy.

17:08.485 --> 17:12.531
- Staying one step ahead of the Russians?
- I expect. Something like that.

17:12.614 --> 17:15.034
- Who's in charge here?
- That'd be Dr. Brenner.

17:15.117 --> 17:16.994
And he builds the space lasers?

17:17.077 --> 17:18.912
- Space lasers?
- Ignore him.

17:18.996 --> 17:20.581
[tape rewinding]

17:21.790 --> 17:24.001
This is the night of the 6th and 7th
we're seeing here?

17:24.084 --> 17:25.419
That's correct.

17:34.219 --> 17:35.345
[tape stops]

17:37.347 --> 17:38.557
Is that it?

17:39.600 --> 17:41.560
Like I said, we would have seen him.

17:44.605 --> 17:47.024
The night of the 7th,
we had a search party out for Will.

17:47.107 --> 17:48.817
You remember anything about that night?

17:48.901 --> 17:51.153
Mmm, not much to remember.
Called it off.

17:51.236 --> 17:53.822
- 'Cause of the storm.
- Yeah, a lot of rain that night.

17:53.906 --> 17:55.574
You see any rain on that tape?

17:56.742 --> 17:58.202
[Powell] What are you thinking?

17:59.536 --> 18:00.829
I don't know.

18:02.790 --> 18:04.041
But they're lying.

18:05.125 --> 18:06.960
[tires screeching]

18:30.109 --> 18:31.735
[low growling]

18:48.752 --> 18:50.504
[growling continues]

19:44.516 --> 19:45.726
[music box chiming]

19:50.439 --> 19:52.191
[lullaby playing]

20:07.206 --> 20:08.457
[lullaby stops]

20:44.117 --> 20:45.744
[indistinct chatter]

20:45.827 --> 20:48.330
[Tommy] That's why science doesn't
make any damn sense to me.

20:48.413 --> 20:51.083
[Carol] No, I swear. Look at this.
It's totally frostbite.

20:51.166 --> 20:54.378
[muffled] Oh, thanks, man.
It's a heated pool.

20:54.461 --> 20:56.296
Well, if it's not frostbite,
then what is it?

20:56.380 --> 20:58.215
Ugh, I don't care what it is,
it's disgusting!

20:58.298 --> 21:00.008
Get it off the table.
We're eating here.

21:00.092 --> 21:01.385
- Ew!
- [Tommy laughs]

21:02.302 --> 21:04.096
Hey, Tommy.

21:04.179 --> 21:06.056
When you left, did you see Barb?

21:06.139 --> 21:08.558
- What?
- Barbara.

21:08.642 --> 21:10.102
She's not here today.

21:10.185 --> 21:13.313
I seriously have no idea
who you're talking about.

21:13.397 --> 21:15.565
Come on, don't be an ass, man.
Did you...

21:15.649 --> 21:17.484
Did you see her leave last night or not?

21:18.360 --> 21:21.196
No, she was gone when we left.

21:21.280 --> 21:23.740
Probably couldn't stand
listening to all that moaning.

21:23.824 --> 21:25.909
- [Tommy chuckles]
- [Carol moaning]

21:25.993 --> 21:27.661
[loudly] Oh, Steve!

21:27.744 --> 21:31.164
- Oh, Steve! Oh, Steve!
- Oh, Steve...

21:31.248 --> 21:33.333
- Oh, Steve!
- [Tommy grunting loudly]

21:33.417 --> 21:35.002
- [mouthing] Okay, chill.
- [both laughing]

21:35.085 --> 21:39.006
Listen... I'm sure she's fine.
She's probably just...

21:39.089 --> 21:41.591
she's probably just, like,
skipping or something.

21:41.675 --> 21:43.093
Yeah.

21:43.176 --> 21:44.761
Yeah, probably.

21:50.726 --> 21:51.768
[indistinct chatter]

22:02.154 --> 22:05.073
- [Mike] How about this one?
- Too big for the sling.

22:06.366 --> 22:09.411
So, do you think Eleven was born
with her powers, like the X-Men,

22:09.494 --> 22:12.789
or do you think she acquired them, like...
like Green Lantern?

22:12.873 --> 22:16.001
She's not a superhero.
She's a weirdo.

22:16.084 --> 22:18.503
Why does that matter?
The X-Men are weirdos.

22:18.587 --> 22:21.048
If you love her so much,
why don't you marry her?

22:21.131 --> 22:22.466
What are you talking about?

22:22.549 --> 22:24.051
- Mike, seriously?
- What?

22:24.134 --> 22:26.178
You look at her all, like...

22:26.261 --> 22:28.722
"Hi, El! El! El! El!

22:28.805 --> 22:30.182
I love you so much!

22:30.265 --> 22:32.100
- Would you marry me?" [exclaiming]
- Shut up, Lucas.

22:32.184 --> 22:33.685
Yeah, shut up, Lucas.

22:34.436 --> 22:36.521
What are you losers
doing back here?

22:36.605 --> 22:38.148
Probably looking for their missing friend.

22:38.231 --> 22:41.151
That's not funny.
It's serious. He's in danger.

22:41.234 --> 22:44.404
I hate to break it to you, Toothless,
but he's not in danger.

22:44.488 --> 22:46.865
He's dead.
That's what my dad says.

22:46.948 --> 22:49.242
He said he was probably killed
by some other queer.

22:49.326 --> 22:50.577
[both laugh]

22:50.660 --> 22:52.412
Come on.
Just ignore them.

22:55.332 --> 22:57.084
- [both laugh]
- [groans]

22:57.167 --> 22:59.294
Watch where you're going, Frogface.

23:00.837 --> 23:02.631
- You all right?
- Yeah.

23:05.175 --> 23:06.343
[sighs]

23:08.261 --> 23:09.930
Hey.

23:10.013 --> 23:11.515
How about this one?

23:12.349 --> 23:15.102
- [chuckles] Yeah.
- Yeah?

23:15.185 --> 23:16.603
Yeah, this is it.

23:16.686 --> 23:18.605
Oh, yeah.

23:18.688 --> 23:21.066
- Yeah, this is the monster killer!
- [Mike laughs]

23:21.149 --> 23:22.192
Whoo!

23:48.426 --> 23:49.427
Hey.

23:50.637 --> 23:52.139
Oh, hey.

24:25.881 --> 24:27.007
[knocking on door]

24:31.219 --> 24:32.220
[sighs]

24:33.346 --> 24:35.265
- Hey!
- Hey, Karen.

24:35.348 --> 24:36.349
Hi...

24:38.935 --> 24:39.978
I brought you a casserole.

24:41.188 --> 24:43.190
Oh! Thank you, uh...

24:44.232 --> 24:46.818
Uh, you wanna... come in?

25:01.041 --> 25:02.042
[Hopper sighs]

25:03.043 --> 25:06.171
Hey, Marissa.
How you doin'?

25:07.631 --> 25:09.633
You have a lot of nerve showing up here.

25:09.716 --> 25:11.051
What?

25:11.134 --> 25:13.136
You could have at least called, said,

25:13.220 --> 25:17.682
"Marissa! Hey, it's not gonna work out.
Sorry I wasted your time. I'm a dick."

25:19.142 --> 25:20.268
Yep.

25:22.938 --> 25:25.315
I'm sorry. Uh...

25:25.398 --> 25:27.776
Maybe we could go out again next week?

25:32.906 --> 25:35.408
Newspapers?
You guys got newspapers around here?

25:36.076 --> 25:38.912
We have the New York Times,
the Post, all the big ones.

25:38.995 --> 25:40.538
Organized by year and topic.

25:40.622 --> 25:43.333
You can find the corresponding microfiche
in the reading room.

25:43.416 --> 25:46.211
Okay, we're looking for anything
on the Hawkins National Laboratory.

25:46.294 --> 25:48.046
Well, shouldn't you be looking
for that missing kid?

25:48.129 --> 25:50.298
Yeah. We are.

25:51.466 --> 25:53.343
Uh, so, why don't you start
with the Times,

25:53.426 --> 25:54.844
and we'll check out the Post.

25:55.929 --> 25:57.097
[scoffs]

26:03.812 --> 26:05.397
The librarian?

26:48.315 --> 26:50.191
[timer ticking]

26:50.275 --> 26:52.902
[Joyce chuckles] Will always loved
Christmas, you know.

26:52.986 --> 26:55.280
So I thought if I...
I put the lights up...

26:56.281 --> 26:57.949
I don't know, he...

26:58.033 --> 26:59.701
I'd feel like he was home somehow.

26:59.784 --> 27:01.286
[stammers] It's silly, I know.

27:01.369 --> 27:04.414
No.
No, it's not silly.

27:04.497 --> 27:06.499
How is Jonathan holding up?

27:06.583 --> 27:09.544
[inhales deeply] You know,
he's good at taking care of himself.

27:09.627 --> 27:11.588
He always has been, you know?

27:11.671 --> 27:12.922
I...

27:13.006 --> 27:16.176
[scoffs] I mean,
he thinks I'm losing my mind, but...

27:18.470 --> 27:19.804
Is something the matter?

27:19.888 --> 27:21.222
Uh, no.

27:21.306 --> 27:22.557
No, I just...

27:22.640 --> 27:24.851
We're having electrical problems.

27:24.934 --> 27:26.061
Joyce.

27:26.644 --> 27:28.563
I want you to know something.

27:28.646 --> 27:31.775
If you need anything, anything at all...

27:31.858 --> 27:33.401
Ted and I are here for you.

27:33.485 --> 27:35.528
[Joyce] Thank you.
Thanks.

27:35.612 --> 27:36.905
Okay.

27:37.989 --> 27:39.741
[Joyce] How... how's Mike
dealing with this?

27:39.824 --> 27:41.618
Is he, uh, okay?

27:41.701 --> 27:44.662
[Karen] Mike?
Uh... I don't know.

27:44.746 --> 27:46.289
He skipped school yesterday.

27:47.332 --> 27:49.334
He's never done anything like that before.

28:14.317 --> 28:15.360
[gasps]

28:15.443 --> 28:16.986
[low growling]

28:27.080 --> 28:30.959
- [timer dings]
- Let me throw in that casserole, okay?

28:33.628 --> 28:35.130
Oh, where's Holly?

28:39.092 --> 28:40.760
[breathing heavily]

28:48.059 --> 28:49.436
[Joyce] Hey!

28:50.019 --> 28:51.187
She shouldn't be here.

28:51.271 --> 28:54.774
Oh, I'm sorry.
She's quite the explorer these days.

28:55.817 --> 28:58.111
- Wait, did you see something?
- Yeah.

28:58.194 --> 28:59.863
What did... what did you see?
Tell me.

28:59.946 --> 29:01.823
- What did you see? What--
- Joyce... Joyce!

29:01.906 --> 29:05.785
Listen... Karen,
thank you for the casserole,

29:05.869 --> 29:07.120
but I need you to leave.

29:07.787 --> 29:08.913
Okay?

29:08.997 --> 29:10.081
[Karen sighs]

29:10.165 --> 29:12.500
- [line ringing]
- Come on, come on, come on...

29:14.294 --> 29:16.546
- [Ms. Holland] Hello?
- Hi.

29:16.629 --> 29:18.506
Hi, uh, Ms. Holland, it's Nancy.

29:18.590 --> 29:19.966
Oh, Nancy, how are you?

29:20.049 --> 29:21.092
Good.
I'm good.

29:21.176 --> 29:24.387
Um, I was just wondering, uh,
is Barb there?

29:24.471 --> 29:26.431
Mmm... No, she hasn't come home yet.

29:27.515 --> 29:29.893
But she did come home, right?
After the vigil?

29:29.976 --> 29:33.229
No, she said she was staying
with you last night.

29:33.313 --> 29:37.108
Right, yes.
She did, sorry.

29:37.192 --> 29:40.361
I meant, did she come home this morning?

29:40.445 --> 29:43.615
I think she left some textbooks
and she was gonna go pick them up.

29:43.698 --> 29:45.909
Oh, um, no, I haven't seen her.

29:46.951 --> 29:50.914
Do-- Do you know what?
I just remembered... she's at the library.

29:50.997 --> 29:54.626
Nancy, will you please have her call me
as soon as you find her?

29:54.709 --> 29:56.669
Yeah.
Yeah, I will.

29:57.879 --> 29:59.088
Sorry to bother you.

30:02.133 --> 30:03.343
[sighs]

30:03.426 --> 30:04.803
[bell rings]

30:12.435 --> 30:14.145
Hey, man.

30:14.229 --> 30:15.271
What's going on?

30:15.355 --> 30:17.357
Nicole here was, uh,
telling us about your work.

30:17.440 --> 30:19.734
[Carol] We've heard great things.
[Tommy] Yeah, sounds cool.

30:19.818 --> 30:23.530
And we'd just love to take a look.
You know, as... connoisseurs of art.

30:23.613 --> 30:25.573
[sighs] I don't know
what you're talking about.

30:25.657 --> 30:26.866
[Steve] Oh, no? Oh...
[Jonathan] Hey.

30:26.950 --> 30:29.160
Please, give me my bag.
No, just...

30:29.244 --> 30:31.704
Man, he is totally trembling.
He must really have something to hide.

30:31.788 --> 30:33.039
Here we go.

30:33.122 --> 30:34.833
Ah...

30:34.916 --> 30:35.917
Here we go.

30:37.460 --> 30:38.711
- Oh, man.
- [Tommy] Let me see.

30:40.547 --> 30:41.548
Dude.

30:41.631 --> 30:43.216
[Tommy exclaims]

30:43.299 --> 30:44.551
[scoffs] Yeah, this isn't creepy at all.

30:44.634 --> 30:46.261
- I was looking for my brother.
- [Steve] No.

30:46.344 --> 30:49.097
No, this is called stalking.
Mmm-hmm.

30:49.722 --> 30:52.433
- What's going on?
- Here's the starring lady.

30:52.517 --> 30:53.643
What?

30:53.726 --> 30:55.770
This creep was spying on us last night.

30:57.063 --> 30:59.107
He was probably gonna
save this one for later.

31:03.152 --> 31:07.657
[Steve clicks tongue] See, you can tell
that he knows it was wrong, but...

31:07.740 --> 31:09.784
Man, that's the thing about perverts...

31:10.827 --> 31:11.828
It's hardwired into 'em.

31:11.911 --> 31:14.789
You know, they just can't help themselves.

31:16.916 --> 31:18.751
- [Tommy laughs]
- [Steve] So...

31:19.919 --> 31:21.546
we'll just have to take away his toy.

31:22.088 --> 31:23.756
- Steve...
- No, please, not the camera.

31:23.840 --> 31:25.550
No, no, wait, wait...
Tommy, Tommy.

31:26.509 --> 31:28.553
- [Tommy chuckles]
- It's okay.

31:29.929 --> 31:31.639
Here you go, man.

31:32.140 --> 31:34.142
[Tommy laughing]

31:36.269 --> 31:38.521
Come on, let's go.
The game's about to start.

31:40.148 --> 31:41.232
Boo.

31:42.609 --> 31:44.611
- [ripping photo]
- [Carol gasps] Bye.

31:59.292 --> 32:01.169
[Steve] Hey, Nance!

32:01.252 --> 32:02.503
Come on.

32:21.230 --> 32:22.982
[breathing heavily]

32:29.197 --> 32:30.365
Three-one-five.

32:31.282 --> 32:33.034
Three-one-five.

32:33.117 --> 32:34.327
[softly] Three-one-five.

32:36.704 --> 32:38.289
[cat meows]

32:41.918 --> 32:43.419
[cat growling]

32:51.135 --> 32:52.679
[hisses]

32:57.892 --> 32:59.018
[cat growls]

32:59.102 --> 33:00.895
[beeping]

33:05.525 --> 33:06.359
[hisses]

33:08.444 --> 33:10.321
[cat snarling]

33:13.366 --> 33:15.910
[cat growling]

33:17.245 --> 33:18.579
[whimpers]

33:27.380 --> 33:29.298
[crying]

33:41.394 --> 33:44.022
No! No!

33:44.105 --> 33:46.399
Papa! Papa!

33:46.482 --> 33:47.775
Papa!

33:47.859 --> 33:49.944
Papa!

33:50.028 --> 33:51.320
[screaming] Papa!

33:52.405 --> 33:54.198
[shrieking]

33:54.991 --> 33:55.992
No!

33:56.075 --> 33:57.243
[shrieking]

34:05.585 --> 34:06.836
[neck snapping]

34:10.006 --> 34:12.050
[panting]

34:44.332 --> 34:45.500
[sobs]

34:47.418 --> 34:48.503
Incredible.

34:51.380 --> 34:52.381
[sniffles]

34:59.305 --> 35:01.599
[sobbing]

35:42.431 --> 35:43.724
[Mike] El!

35:45.685 --> 35:47.228
[panting] You okay?

35:49.647 --> 35:51.607
Hop on.
We only have a few hours.

36:02.493 --> 36:05.079
So, I told Mr. Mundy...

36:05.163 --> 36:08.249
"The solution of ten plus Y equals...

36:08.332 --> 36:09.709
- blow me."
- [Tommy laughing]

36:09.792 --> 36:12.128
[Steve] Bull, if you did that,
you'd be in detention right now.

36:12.211 --> 36:13.671
Saturday.

36:13.754 --> 36:15.548
[Tommy] I bet Mr. Mundy's still a virgin.

36:15.631 --> 36:16.757
[Carol] Oh, he's so a virgin!

36:16.841 --> 36:19.760
Maybe you should blow him, Carol.
Help your grades a bit.

36:19.844 --> 36:21.220
[chuckling]

36:21.679 --> 36:22.805
Whoa, Nance, where you going?

36:22.889 --> 36:25.433
[Nancy stammering] I totally forgot.

36:25.516 --> 36:27.101
I told my mom I would, um...

36:27.185 --> 36:28.644
I would do something with her.

36:28.728 --> 36:30.605
Well, what do you mean?
The game's about to start.

36:30.688 --> 36:32.148
I'm sorry.

36:33.524 --> 36:36.152
[sighs] What the hell's wrong with her?

36:36.235 --> 36:39.197
Maybe she freaked out
when you went all psycho on the psycho.

36:39.280 --> 36:40.281
Oh, give me a break.

36:40.364 --> 36:42.658
[Carol] What'd you expect,
dating Miss Perfect?

36:49.207 --> 36:50.666
Why did they hurt you?

36:51.834 --> 36:52.877
What?

36:55.338 --> 36:56.464
Oh, that.

36:56.547 --> 36:57.548
Uh...

36:57.632 --> 36:59.300
I just fell at recess.

37:00.801 --> 37:02.428
- Mike...
- Yeah?

37:02.511 --> 37:03.971
Friends tell the truth.

37:06.057 --> 37:07.099
[Mike sighs]

37:07.183 --> 37:10.019
I was tripped by this mouth breather,
Troy, okay?

37:10.102 --> 37:11.562
Mouth breather?

37:11.687 --> 37:13.564
Yeah, you know...

37:13.648 --> 37:14.774
a dumb person.

37:14.857 --> 37:16.025
A knucklehead.

37:16.108 --> 37:17.193
[Eleven] Knucklehead?

37:18.819 --> 37:21.906
I don't know why I just didn't tell you.
Everyone at school knows.

37:21.989 --> 37:24.825
I just didn't want you to think
I was such a wastoid, you know?

37:24.909 --> 37:27.036
- Mike...
- Yeah?

37:27.119 --> 37:28.621
I understand.

37:29.538 --> 37:30.957
Oh.

37:31.040 --> 37:32.792
Okay, cool.

37:32.875 --> 37:34.085
Cool.

37:56.315 --> 37:57.483
Barb?

37:59.652 --> 38:00.987
Barb!

38:19.380 --> 38:20.715
Barb?

38:23.259 --> 38:24.593
[rustling]

38:31.350 --> 38:32.727
Barb?

38:48.034 --> 38:49.327
[rustling]

38:50.202 --> 38:51.495
Barb?

38:52.121 --> 38:53.414
[growling]

38:53.497 --> 38:54.498
Oh!

38:56.625 --> 38:58.002
[panting]

39:01.839 --> 39:03.924
[porch swing creaking]

39:08.095 --> 39:09.221
[dog whines]

39:10.389 --> 39:12.892
[barking]

39:55.684 --> 39:56.727
[sighs]

40:04.527 --> 40:05.611
[sniffles]

40:06.821 --> 40:09.573
Will... are you here?

40:11.742 --> 40:13.119
[exclaims]

40:13.202 --> 40:15.037
Okay, good, good, good, good.

40:15.955 --> 40:16.997
Are you...

40:17.081 --> 40:21.127
Um, blink once for yes, twice for no.

40:21.210 --> 40:23.671
[stammers] Can you do that for me,
sweetie?

40:23.754 --> 40:24.797
Can you do...

40:27.091 --> 40:29.593
[exclaims] Oh, good boy.
Good boy.

40:30.594 --> 40:32.805
[crying] Baby, I need to know...

40:33.973 --> 40:36.434
[exhales heavily] Are you alive?

40:40.062 --> 40:41.272
[sighing]

40:44.233 --> 40:45.693
[softly] Are you safe?

40:50.781 --> 40:52.199
[exclaims]

40:56.579 --> 41:00.124
I need to know where to find you, honey.
Where... where are you?

41:00.207 --> 41:03.669
Can you...
can you tell me where you are?

41:03.752 --> 41:05.087
Can you...

41:06.005 --> 41:09.758
[whimpering] Please, baby.
I need to find you. Tell me what to do.

41:12.052 --> 41:13.721
[voice breaking] Please just...

41:13.804 --> 41:14.805
[mutters]

41:16.807 --> 41:18.142
Will...

41:21.812 --> 41:23.189
[sniffling]

41:44.877 --> 41:47.296
Hey! You're home early!
How was the game?

41:50.090 --> 41:52.718
Nancy?
What's the matter?

41:53.636 --> 41:54.887
[crying] It's Barb.

41:54.970 --> 41:56.180
I think...

41:57.598 --> 41:59.475
something happened.

41:59.558 --> 42:02.478
[sniffles] Something terrible.

42:04.605 --> 42:05.898
[Powell] I don't know, Chief.

42:05.981 --> 42:07.233
What don't you know?

42:07.316 --> 42:10.486
This lady, Terry Ives,
sounds like a real nut to me.

42:10.569 --> 42:14.615
Her kid was taken
for LSD mind control experiments?

42:14.698 --> 42:15.783
She's been discredited.

42:15.866 --> 42:16.951
- [sighs]
- Claim was thrown out--

42:17.034 --> 42:18.160
Okay, forget about her.

42:18.953 --> 42:20.496
Take a look at this.

42:20.579 --> 42:22.790
- Dr. Martin Brenner.
- Who?

42:22.873 --> 42:24.500
Brenner.

42:24.583 --> 42:26.502
He runs Hawkins Lab.

42:26.585 --> 42:27.628
Okay.

42:28.963 --> 42:31.215
[scoffs] You don't find that interesting?

42:31.298 --> 42:32.716
Not really.

42:32.800 --> 42:35.678
He was involved in some hippie crap
back in the day, so what?

42:35.761 --> 42:39.932
No, this isn't hippie crap.
This is CIA-sanctioned research.

42:40.015 --> 42:42.142
Doesn't mean he had
anything to do with our kid.

42:42.226 --> 42:45.229
Come on. Look at that.
Hospital gowns. All of 'em.

42:45.312 --> 42:47.523
Now, that piece of fabric
that the teacher found by the pipe.

42:47.606 --> 42:49.525
That sure looked
like a hospital gown to me, huh?

42:49.608 --> 42:52.027
- Am I wrong?
- I don't know, Chief.

42:52.111 --> 42:53.445
[sighs] Come on, man.

42:53.529 --> 42:55.823
Work with me here.

42:55.906 --> 42:58.492
I'm not saying that there's
some grand conspiracy.

42:58.576 --> 42:59.827
I'm just...

43:02.204 --> 43:03.289
[sighs]

43:04.248 --> 43:05.958
I'm saying maybe something happened.

43:07.042 --> 43:10.879
Maybe Will was in the wrong place
at the wrong time

43:10.963 --> 43:12.881
and he saw something
that he shouldn't have.

43:14.091 --> 43:16.635
- It's a reach.
- It's a start.

43:16.719 --> 43:19.263
[Callahan] Hey, Powell,
is the chief with you?

43:20.014 --> 43:21.557
Hopper here.
What do you got?

43:32.359 --> 43:33.861
[siren blaring]

44:05.100 --> 44:06.185
[Eleven] Here.

44:06.268 --> 44:08.812
Yeah, this is where Will lives.

44:09.355 --> 44:10.439
Hiding.

44:10.522 --> 44:13.150
No, no, this is where he lives.

44:13.233 --> 44:15.235
He's missing from here.
Understand?

44:18.364 --> 44:20.783
- [Lucas] What are we doing here?
- She said he's hiding here.

44:20.866 --> 44:22.576
Um... no!

44:22.660 --> 44:25.329
I swear, if we walked
all the way out here for nothing--

44:25.412 --> 44:26.914
That's exactly what we did.

44:26.997 --> 44:30.042
I told you she didn't know
what the hell she was talking about!

44:31.043 --> 44:32.836
- Why did you bring us here?
- [stammers]

44:32.920 --> 44:36.131
- Mike, don't waste your time with her.
- What do you want to do then?

44:36.215 --> 44:37.800
Call the cops,
like we should have done yesterday.

44:37.883 --> 44:39.468
- We are not calling the cops!
- [Dustin] Hey, guys?

44:39.551 --> 44:41.762
- What other choice do we have?
- Guys!

44:41.845 --> 44:43.597
[sirens approaching]

44:50.312 --> 44:51.688
[Mike] Will...

45:06.412 --> 45:07.955
[exhales]

45:09.915 --> 45:10.999
Okay.

45:11.083 --> 45:13.419
Okay, baby, talk to me.

45:13.502 --> 45:15.212
Talk to me.
Where are you?

45:16.588 --> 45:18.882
"R." Good, good, good, good.

45:18.966 --> 45:20.342
That's good.
Come on, come on.

45:20.926 --> 45:22.177
"I...

45:22.886 --> 45:24.388
G...

45:24.471 --> 45:26.140
H... T...

45:26.849 --> 45:28.100
H...

45:28.183 --> 45:29.184
E...

45:29.309 --> 45:31.311
R... E..."

45:31.395 --> 45:32.980
"Right here."

45:33.981 --> 45:35.107
"Right here"?

45:35.190 --> 45:37.860
[stammers] I don't know what that means.

45:37.943 --> 45:40.237
I need you to tell me what to do.

45:40.320 --> 45:41.321
What should I do?

45:41.405 --> 45:44.658
How do I get to you? How do I find you?
What should I do?

45:55.335 --> 45:57.588
[gasping]

45:59.256 --> 46:00.340
[Joyce whimpers]

46:05.095 --> 46:07.139
[monster screeching]

46:08.348 --> 46:10.309
[sirens wailing]

46:51.975 --> 46:53.143
[Hopper] Oh, Jesus.

46:59.316 --> 47:00.943
[panting]

47:01.026 --> 47:03.403
Oh, God.
Please tell me it's not the kid.

47:03.487 --> 47:05.531
[indistinct radio chatter]

47:19.878 --> 47:21.922
[breathing heavily]

47:31.390 --> 47:34.351
It's not Will.
It can't be.

47:42.901 --> 47:45.487
It's Will.
It's really Will.

47:52.244 --> 47:53.412
[Eleven] Mike...

47:53.495 --> 47:55.664
- "Mike"? "Mike," what?
- [gasps]

47:55.747 --> 47:57.874
You were supposed to help us
find him alive.

47:57.958 --> 47:59.376
You said he was alive!

47:59.459 --> 48:00.877
Why did you lie to us?

48:01.670 --> 48:03.171
What's wrong with you?

48:03.255 --> 48:05.007
What is wrong with you?

48:05.674 --> 48:07.301
- [softly] Mike...
- What?

48:10.679 --> 48:13.223
Mike, come on.
Don't do this, man.

48:13.307 --> 48:14.349
Mike...

48:14.433 --> 48:17.102
Mike, where are you going?
Mike!

48:22.024 --> 48:23.275
[Lucas] Mike!

48:30.532 --> 48:31.908
[shrieks]

48:33.619 --> 48:35.287
- [Joyce gasps]
- [Jonathan] Mom?

48:36.997 --> 48:39.249
- Mom, what happened?
- [Joyce whimpers]

48:39.333 --> 48:40.584
[Jonathan] It's okay.

48:41.752 --> 48:42.919
Hey.

48:48.258 --> 48:49.509
[Karen] Michael?

48:51.261 --> 48:52.471
What's wrong?

49:03.815 --> 49:05.817
[sobbing]

49:19.873 --> 49:21.833
[sirens wailing]
